Feature: What a drone knows on board
  A drone knows what its own camera sees, also when it is out of contact. The commander does not
  know it: a drone in a radio shadow sends no camera picture. The camera sees 150 m round the
  drone. It shows the enemy drones that are in that range, and who holds a tower that is
  in that range. The drone also knows its [[battery]] and the time since it was last in contact.

  This is all that a drone can use to decide for itself. A decision that needs more is a decision
  for the commander, taken before the drone goes dark.

  Expectation: A drone out of contact sees the enemy drones near it
    Given the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the first Blue drone is near the Red home tower
    And the Red scout is 50 m from the first Blue drone
    Then the enemy drones on board the first Blue drone are 1
    And the Red scout on the Blue map is unknown

  Expectation: A drone does not see an enemy drone that is far
    Overrides: A drone out of contact sees the enemy drones near it
    The Red scout is far from the first Blue drone.

    Given the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the first Blue drone is near the Red home tower
    And the Red scout is far from anything Blue
    Then the enemy drones on board the first Blue drone are 0

  Expectation: A drone sees who holds the tower in its camera
    The Blue map shows the holder of the west tower as the team last saw it. The drone sees it now.

    Given the west tower is held by Red
    And the first Blue drone is in the west circle
    And the Red drones in the west circle are 0
    And the Blue drones in the west circle are 1
    Then the west tower on board the first Blue drone is held by Red

  Expectation: A drone knows how long it has been out of contact
    Given the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the first Blue drone is near the Red home tower
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the time out of contact on board the first Blue drone is 10 s
